            <div class="tip-icon"><i class="ri-check-line"></i></div>
            <div>
              <h6 class="mb-1 font-weight-bold">Keep It Short, Punchy &amp; Pronounceable</h6>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Short domains under 12 characters are easier to remember, reduce typing errors on mobile keyboards, and make word-of-mouth recommendations frictionless.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pillar-tip-item d-flex gap-3 mb-3">
            <div class="tip-icon"><i class="ri-check-line"></i></div>
            <div>
              <h6 class="mb-1 font-weight-bold">Avoid Hyphens and Confusing Numbers</h6>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Search engines and users perceive hyphenated domains as low-quality. A clean, single-word or compound brandable domain projects established authority.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pillar-tip-item d-flex gap-3 mb-3">
            <div class="tip-icon"><i class="ri-check-line"></i></div>
            <div>
              <h6 class="mb-1 font-weight-bold">Target Local SEO with Strategic ccTLDs</h6>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">If your audience is in India, a <strong>.in</strong> or <strong>.co.in</strong> extension signals geographic relevance directly to Google India, giving you an edge in local search queries.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pillar-tip-item d-flex gap-3">
            <div class="tip-icon"><i class="ri-check-line"></i></div>
            <div>
              <h6 class="mb-1 font-weight-bold">Leave Room for Product Expansion</h6>
              <p class="small text-muted mb-0">Avoid names that are too narrow (like <em>cheapshoesdelhi.com</em>). Choose a flexible brandable name (like <em>stepcraft.in</em>) that can grow into multiple product categories.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
